-- Quality Monitoring Agent -- Layer 1 (Operational Health).
--
-- NOTE (Week 2): the SUPPORTED standalone variant is now quality_monitor.tql
-- (own namespace, senses the target cross-app over mon/REST, no cross-app
-- stream references). This file remains the combined-app pointer and the
-- postmortem/recovery reference for the original separate-app attempt.
--
-- DEFAULT PATH: Layer 1 now ships INSIDE qualitydemo.FareInference
-- (striim/pipeline/inference_pipeline.tql). Deploy that one app and the agent
-- comes with it, branching off ScoredStream in-scope. Use that, not this file,
-- for the demo.
--
-- This file is kept for two purposes: (1) RECOVERY from the failed separate-app
-- attempt below, and (2) a REFERENCE separate-app variant for when Layers 2/3
-- grow enough to warrant their own application lifecycle.
--
-- WHY a separate app failed: a stream is only visible at CREATE time within the
-- application (and namespace) that defines it. An OP in app B doing
-- "FROM qualitydemo.ScoredStream" gets "Stream not found" unless ScoredStream
-- already exists, and cross-namespace stream consumption is not reliable. The
-- robust pattern is the combined app (above). If you do split later, define the
-- agent app in the SAME namespace (qualitydemo) and deploy FareInference FIRST.

-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- RECOVERY: drop the half-created app from a failed separate-app run.
-- (It only got as far as CREATE APPLICATION + the stream before the OP failed,
-- so it is not deployed; DROP is enough.)
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- DROP APPLICATION quality.QualityMonitor CASCADE;
-- DROP NAMESPACE quality CASCADE;

-- ======================================================================
-- REFERENCE ONLY -- separate-app variant. Do NOT run alongside the combined
-- app in inference_pipeline.tql (that would double-register the agent OP and
-- its streams). Requires qualitydemo.FareInference DEPLOYED first.
-- ======================================================================
-- USE qualitydemo;
--
-- CREATE STREAM HealthAssessmentStream OF Global.WAEvent;
--
-- CREATE OPEN PROCESSOR HealthAgent USING Global.ModelQualityAgent (
--   TargetNamespace: 'qualitydemo',
--   TargetAppName: 'FareInference',
--   TickIntervalSec: 30,
--   EnableLogging: true
-- )
-- INSERT INTO HealthAssessmentStream
-- FROM qualitydemo.ScoredStream;   -- resolves only if FareInference is deployed
--
-- CREATE TARGET HealthSysOut USING Global.SysOut ( name: 'QualityMonitor-Layer1' )
-- INPUT FROM HealthAssessmentStream;
